id: pm-gh1078
title: "GH-1078: Complete-list certification accepts absent or contradictory truth receipts and emits stale recovery"
description: "The public certifyCompleteListResult SDK primitive in 2026.8.21 can issue a complete_list certificate when omission_receipt or read_output is absent, when completeness reports unreadable rows, or when omission fields contradict has_omissions=false. PmCompleteListValidationError also recommends deprecated list-all recovery without the current unbounded output-limit/include controls. This is the GitHub #1078 follow-on to the shipped fail-closed complete-list lineage in pm-y4aaol and belongs under the SDK-first architecture epic pm-usfg."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:query","area:sdk",complete-list,context-integrity,recovery
created_at: "2026-08-21T12:55:33.362Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T18:00:06.839Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T18:00:06.290Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T18:00:06.290Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Require completeness.status=complete with safe-integer zero unreadable counts; require omission_receipt has_omissions=false, safe-integer zero count, and empty groups; require read_output contract v1 for list with within_budget=true, no compaction or omission, and complete include/amount/cost dimensions; reject output budget truncation/exceeded disclosures; return stable independent finding codes with absent, malformed, contradictory, and nonzero negative controls; emit canonical executable current recovery and prove it in a fresh-tracker acceptance test"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1078
severity: high
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21 public SDK
repro_steps: "Obtain the real pm list --all strict unbounded JSON envelope, then independently delete omission_receipt, contradict its count/groups, delete read_output, or set completeness unreadable_item_count=1; certifyCompleteListResult currently accepts each mutated envelope. Inspect PmCompleteListValidationError.recovery.suggested_retry for stale list-all syntax."
resolution: "Resolved: complete-list certification fails closed on missing or inconsistent completeness receipts and supplies an executable strict unbounded recovery."
expected_result: "Certification fails closed unless completeness, omission_receipt, and read_output independently prove complete unbounded delivery with stable finding codes; budget truncation disclosures are rejected; the canonical suggested retry uses list --all, output-include full, output-budget unbounded, and output-limit unbounded and executes successfully in a fresh tracker."
actual_result: Missing or contradictory truth receipts are accepted and certified; recovery suggests pm list-all --full --strict-read --no-truncate --output-budget unbounded --json.
affected_version: 2026.8.21
component: SDK complete-list certification
regression: true
